# Billing regression safety

- Treat `docs/DEMO_REQUIREMENTS.md` as the current product/billing source of
  truth. Treat `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` as historical when they conflict.
- Before changing packages, contracts, usage, balances, invoices, checkout,
  credit purchase, auto top-up, customer state, or seeding, read the applicable
  sections of `docs/REGRESSION_CHECKLIST.md`.
- Changes in shared billing/customer code require review of both AI Builder
  (USD credits) and Generation (custom credits), including legacy Generation
  contracts that still use `USD (cents)`.
- Validate transition changes against both exact-time behavior and the
  temporary legacy hour-boundary fallback. Never mask misattributed usage with
  a compensating credit.
- Use a fresh customer for end-to-end attribution checks; historical usage
  cannot validate a corrected contract transition.
- Never edit or overwrite `.env`.
- In handoff, distinguish uncommitted work, local commits, GitHub pushes, and
  tags. Do not describe the tree as clean without checking `git status`.
